\description{
Biallelic genotypes at chosen loci for chosen genomes, painted on the genealogy the run recorded.
The model carries no mutation, so a run's genomes differ only by descent: at every position each
genome descends from exactly one \strong{root genome}, a day-1 founder template or an imported genome,
and root genomes are unrelated. Each root genome draws its allele at each locus independently, ALT
with probability \code{plaf}, and every genome carries the allele of the root genome it descends from
there. \code{roots} records that root genome for every genome and locus, the truth behind the calls:
two genomes share a root genome at a locus exactly where \code{\link[=ibd_segments]{ibd_segments()}} finds them sharing a
common ancestor.
}
\details{
Each genome can be its own sample (a clone), or the genomes can be grouped into host samples by
\code{sample_id}, as a blood sample holds every clone in the host: a host call is 0 when every clone
carries REF, 1 when every one carries ALT, and 0.5 when both are present.
}
\section{Reproducibility}{

The root genomes' alleles are drawn first, for every root genome of the run and every locus, so with
one seed, run and loci a genome's alleles do not depend on which other genomes are asked for, how
they are grouped, or the error and missingness rates; then the errors, then the missing calls.
Large sets of genomes can therefore be genotyped in batches with one seed, and several error rates
laid over one truth. A number in \code{seed} seeds this call alone and leaves the session's random
stream as it was; \code{NULL} draws from the session's stream.
}

\section{What painting leaves out}{

Root genomes are unrelated, so there is no background relatedness or linkage disequilibrium among
them; imports draw from the same frequencies as the founders; an allele never changes along the
genealogy; a host sample records which alleles are present, not their proportions; loci are
biallelic; and \code{plaf} is the frequency among the root genomes, which drifts among the genomes
sampled later.
}

\section{Which genomes can be genotyped}{

Any genome in the tree sequence: case clones, hypnozoite batches and mosquito products alike. A
run with \code{RETAIN_FULL_HISTORY = FALSE} records only the genomes alive at its end; a run that never
started holds none.
}

\section{Python}{

The IBD and ARG functions read a run's tree sequence with Python's tskit, through the
reticulate package. Either of two routes works. \emph{Automatic}: with no Python chosen, reticulate
sets up its own environment with tskit (>= 1.0) and numpy the first time one of these
functions runs; this needs internet once. \emph{Your own Python}: set \code{RETICULATE_PYTHON} to a
Python that has those modules (in \verb{~/.Renviron} to keep it) before the first such call of a
session. A function that cannot reach them stops with an error of class
\code{malariafwd_no_python} that says what to do, and \code{\link[=check_setup]{check_setup()}} reports what is found.
}

